Source: firehpc
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: HPCKit team <maintainers@hpck.it>
Homepage: https://github.com/rackslab/firehpc
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 bash-completion,
 python3-all (>= 3.6),
 python3-setuptools,
 python3-ansible-runner,
 python3-dasbus,
 python3-fake-factory,
 python3-paramiko,
 python3-racksdb,
{% if version.dist == "ubuntu2204" %}
 python3-rfl-build,
{% endif %}
 dh-python,
 pybuild-plugin-pyproject,
 asciidoctor,
Standards-Version: 4.2.1

Package: firehpc
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3-firehpc (= ${binary:Version}),
 firehpc-agent (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-ansible-runner,
 python3-fake-factory,
 python3-jinja2,
 python3-paramiko,
 python3-racksdb,
 python3-venv,
 python3-yaml,
Description: Deploy container-based emulated HPC clusters
 FireHPC is an open source solution to deploy container-based emulated HPC
 clusters, typically for development, testing or learning purposes.
 This package provides FireHPC CLI.

Package: firehpc-agent
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3-firehpc (= ${binary:Version}),
 polkitd,
 systemd-container,
 systemd-resolved,
Recommends:
 libnss-mymachines,
Description: Agent to run containers of emulated HPC clusters
 FireHPC is an open source solution to deploy container-based emulated HPC
 clusters, typically for development, testing or learning purposes.
 This package provides FireHPC agent and system files (systemd services,
 wrappers, polkit rules) required to run clusters containers on the host,
 locally or on behalf of FireHPC running on another host.

Package: firehpc-nvidia-fake
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Description: Fake NVIDIA tools for FireHPC emulated GPU nodes
 FireHPC is an open source solution to deploy container-based emulated HPC
 clusters, typically for development, testing or learning purposes.
 This package provides fake nvidia-smi and NVIDIA DCGM exporter programs to
 emulate NVIDIA GPUs on emulated cluster compute nodes, for GPU monitoring
 tools such as CEEMS exporter. It does not depend on FireHPC library and it
 is meant to be installed on cluster nodes.

Package: python3-firehpc
Architecture: all
Section: python
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3-dasbus,
Description: Python library for container-based emulated HPC clusters
 FireHPC is an open source solution to deploy container-based emulated HPC
 clusters, typically for development, testing or learning purposes.
 This package provides FireHPC Python library.
